4. Compatibility with MIT
--------------------------------------------------------------------------

MIT, BSD, Apache-2.0 and HPND components are permissive and compatible.
MPL-2.0 is file-level copyleft and compatible with an MIT-licensed
application when the MPL files are used unmodified (our case).
LGPL libraries are compatible when used as unmodified, replaceable libraries
(our case). The licenses of bundled components must be kept with any
redistribution (this file and libs/LICENSE-LibreHardwareMonitor.txt).
This is an engineering summary, not legal advice.
